code s).length % 8 = 0`.\n   - `encode_valid_chars_prop` / `encode_valid_chars_thm`: Output characters belong to `_b32alphabet` or `'='`, are valid ASCII (`< 128`), and satisfy `isValidBase32 (b32encode s) false none = true`.\n   - `encode_padding_prop` / `encode_padding_thm`: Exact decomposition into unpadded Base32 digits followed by `padCount (s.length % 5)` `'='` bytes, and exact recovery via `rstripEq`.\n   - `encode_append_mult5_prop` / `encode_append_mult5_thm`: 5-byte block homomorphism (`s1.length % 5 = 0 → b32encode (s1 ++ s2) = b32encode s1 ++ b32encode s2`).\n   - `decode_encode_roundtrip_prop` / `decode_encode_roundtrip_thm`: Full round-trip left-inverse proofs `b32decode? (b32encode s) false none = some s` and `b32decode (b32encode s) false none = s`.\n   - `encode_injective_prop` / `encode_injective_thm`: Injectivity of `b32encode`.\n   - `decode_casefold_prop` / `decode_casefold_thm`: Case-insensitive decoding on normal and lowercased encodings.\n   - `decode_map01_prop` / `decode_map01_thm`: Equivalence of `map01` parameter handling with `'0' → 'O'` and `'1' → m` pre-mapping.\n   - `decode_valid_length_prop` / `decode_valid_length_thm`: Error characterization (`b32decode? s casefold map01 = none ↔ isValidBase32 s casefold map01 = false`) and decoded output length formula.\n   - `Post_prop` & `correctness_thm`: Main correctness theorem `Pre s → Post_prop s`.\n\n4. **Imperative Implementation & Equivalence** ([23_base32.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/23_base32.lean#L950-L1149)):\n   - Implemented `b32encode_imp`, `b32decode?_imp`, and `b32decode_imp` using `Id.run do` with mutable state and proven `b32encode_equiv_thm`, `b32decode?_equiv_thm`, and `b32decode_equiv_thm`.","thinking":"Examining the output reveals a comprehensive set of theorems associated with a specific module. These theorems cover core functionalities like encoding and decoding, base conversion characteristics, padding mechanisms, and roundtrip verification. The analysis suggests a strong focus on ensuring the integrity and correctness of the encoding/decoding processes within the module.\n\n\n"}
